We can express that mechanism cautiously as: $O_{\mathrm{sustained}}
\sim
E_{\mathrm{work}}\cdot C_{\mathrm{maintained}}.$ Here $O_{\mathrm{sustained}}$ means durable output, $E_{\mathrm{work}}$ means direct work effort, and $C_{\mathrm{maintained}}$ means the maintained capacity of the person doing the work. The equation is not in the interview. It is a bookkeeping shorthand for the logic the interview states in practical language.

